    "media:imagetext": "DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE\nREGULATION\n\"Air Commerce Regulations\", Dec. 31, 1926 -\nSection 19.\n(B)\n1.\nTake-off within 1,000 feet.\n2. Climb\nat least 250 feet the first minute\n3.\nafter taking off.\nLand, coming to full stop without external\naid, within 1,000 feet from where the\nwheels first\ntouch the landing area.\nAirplane specifications by manufacturers -\n(1) Fairchild Cabin Monoplane FC-2\nGross Weight 2700 lbs.\nClimb 1,000 feet 1 minute with full load.\n(2) Fairchild Cabin Monoplane FC-2\nGross weight 3275 Ibs.\nClimb 650 feet per minute with full load.\n(3) Fokker Trimotor FVI1, Commerical Transport.\nClimb 720 feet per minute with full load.\n(4) Travel Air Monoplane•\nClimb 650 feet per minute with full load.\n(5) Waco Airplane\nClimb 1,000 to 1,500 feet per minute.\n(6) American Eagle\n• Climb 500 feet per minute.\n(7) Ryan M-2 and also Ryan Broughm.\nClimb 1,000 feet in first minute.\n(8) Curtiss.\nArmy Pursuit Ship P.w. 8\nClimb 1,850 feet per minute.\n(9) Swallow\nClimb 600 feet per minute\n(10) Martin, Commercial Model 70 plane.\nClimb 800 feet per minute\n11) Eaglerock, o place.\nimb 600 feet ner minute full Load.",
